 "title": "Controls",
 "summary": "The controls: an IK handle out of each foot and a pole vector above each knee (disconnected, not deforming); each lower leg gets an IK constraint (chain 2, pole angle set so the leg keeps its rest shape) and each pole follows its handle. The old root becomes 'body', a new root sits on the floor, the IK handles follow the root and the body follows the root, so the body can dance while the feet stay planted. The neck gets an IK handle above the head (chain of 7, with a pole), following the body. Tried out: body lowered and turned, a foot lifted, the head pulled aside.",
